for discharge at a potential of about –40 millivolts. Then, 
the entire process begins again: self- excitation to cause 
the <span class="c-yellow">action potential</span>, recovery from the <span class="c-yellow">action potential</span>, 
hyperpolarization after the <span class="c-yellow">action potential</span> is over, drift of 
